1
00:00:00,259 --> 00:00:01,259
[This is a fictional story. All characters
and events bear no relation to reality]

2
00:00:01,259 --> 00:00:02,259
[Child and animal scenes filmed safely]

3
00:00:02,259 --> 00:00:03,332
[under the guardian
and expert supervision per guidelines]

4
00:00:03,332 --> 00:00:05,559
[2018 South Korea vs. Germany match]

5
00:00:05,559 --> 00:00:08,092
Republic of Korea!

6
00:00:09,079 --> 00:00:10,792
Republic of Korea!

7
00:00:10,792 --> 00:00:12,526
[Korea, toward victory]

8
00:00:12,526 --> 00:00:14,759
[Korea! Let the victory chants ring out!]
Republic of Korea!

9
00:00:15,892 --> 00:00:16,892
[Episode 7]

10
00:00:16,892 --> 00:00:21,392
Pickpockets taking advantage
of the World Cup crowds in the square!

11
00:00:22,231 --> 00:00:24,426
Pickpocket! Pickpocket!

12
00:00:26,767 --> 00:00:30,287
I do like soccer,
but I'm really not here to have fun.

13
00:00:30,287 --> 00:00:31,523
Who knows?

14
00:00:31,523 --> 00:00:34,092
Maybe I'll even get a shot
for a police sketch, huh?

15
00:00:37,555 --> 00:00:41,392
I've got the bait set up
absolutely perfectly.

16
00:00:44,351 --> 00:00:45,526
I'm hanging up.

17
00:00:45,526 --> 00:00:49,159
Hey, you in the red cap, stop!

18
00:00:51,991 --> 00:00:53,759
That one is a fake.

19
00:00:55,033 --> 00:00:57,526
The real one, loaded with cash, is this.

20
00:00:58,533 --> 00:01:00,233
Darn it!

21
00:01:03,039 --> 00:01:05,291
Darn it!

22
00:01:05,291 --> 00:01:09,059
If you don't want your picture taken,
at least give me an interview!

23
00:01:10,123 --> 00:01:13,531
The old man told me
to keep a low profile for a while.

24
00:01:13,531 --> 00:01:15,847
You know I always listen to my backer.

25
00:01:15,847 --> 00:01:19,807
<i>Hey, I heard that dead delivery guy
was a widower with kids.</i>

26
00:01:19,807 --> 00:01:22,991
<i>Man, of all people, you had to hit
a guy like that with your car?</i>

27
00:01:22,991 --> 00:01:25,091
Hey, what on earth are you talking about?

28
00:01:25,091 --> 00:01:29,307
The whole front end of
my 300-million-won babe got wrecked.

29
00:01:29,307 --> 00:01:30,943
I'm the victim here.

30
00:01:30,943 --> 00:01:33,567
<i>Hey, we scored! We scored!</i>

31
00:01:33,567 --> 00:01:36,131
Jeez, so what?

32
00:01:36,131 --> 00:01:37,831
Hello?

33
00:01:41,271 --> 00:01:45,759
Oh, my, these darn things
are pissing me off so much.

34
00:01:46,687 --> 00:01:50,392
Oh, it's Dumbass Korea, you punks!

35
00:02:21,023 --> 00:02:22,723
Meeting concluded.

36
00:02:24,250 --> 00:02:25,950
<i>Is it over?</i>

37
00:02:27,851 --> 00:02:29,747
It's finally over.

38
00:02:29,747 --> 00:02:31,287
Relax, rookie.

39
00:02:31,287 --> 00:02:33,259
Get that cramp out of your leg too.

40
00:02:33,259 --> 00:02:36,259
Pardon? I wasn't nervous or anything...

41
00:02:41,959 --> 00:02:44,559
Half of a meeting is just waiting.

42
00:02:45,271 --> 00:02:46,911
So what does that require?

43
00:02:46,911 --> 00:02:49,011
Endurance.

44
00:02:49,011 --> 00:02:51,471
I should work on my strength.

45
00:02:51,471 --> 00:02:53,492
Good work, Ms. Yoo.

46
00:02:55,305 --> 00:02:58,167
You did a pretty good job too.

47
00:02:58,167 --> 00:02:59,875
I can leave with peace of mind.

48
00:02:59,875 --> 00:03:01,339
What?

49
00:03:01,339 --> 00:03:03,875
Leave? Where? Who's leaving?

50
00:03:03,875 --> 00:03:06,926
Excellent work for your first meeting.
Good job.

51
00:03:09,155 --> 00:03:11,355
Take the emergency stairs down
to the first floor.

52
00:03:11,355 --> 00:03:14,591
Exit through Gate 3 and blend into the crowd.

53
00:03:14,591 --> 00:03:16,291
Okay.

54
00:03:19,983 --> 00:03:21,975
But you can't watch the soccer match.
What are you going to do?

55
00:03:21,975 --> 00:03:23,511
<i>I'm not interested.</i>

56
00:03:23,511 --> 00:03:25,526
Really? That's unusual.

57
00:03:25,526 --> 00:03:27,511
<i>You're not interested either.</i>

58
00:03:27,511 --> 00:03:29,851
That's why you scheduled
a meeting on a day like this.

59
00:03:29,851 --> 00:03:33,426
Hey, that's because today is
a good day to hold a meeting.

60
00:03:34,895 --> 00:03:36,191
But, Ms. Yoo,

61
00:03:36,191 --> 00:03:41,259
do you have any interest in
anything besides work?

62
00:03:48,235 --> 00:03:50,927
Have you picked up any movement right now?

63
00:03:50,927 --> 00:03:52,257
Around the emergency stairs.

64
00:03:52,257 --> 00:03:53,957
<i>Pardon?</i>

65
00:03:57,703 --> 00:03:58,703
No.

66
00:03:58,703 --> 00:04:01,851
Other than the security office,
the whole building is empty.

67
00:04:01,851 --> 00:04:04,215
Then rewind and see if we missed anything.

68
00:04:04,215 --> 00:04:05,587
Since I came upstairs.

69
00:04:05,587 --> 00:04:06,995
Is something wrong?

70
00:04:06,995 --> 00:04:08,695
Let me know if you find something.

71
00:04:37,592 --> 00:04:40,959
[Kwon Tae Seong]

72
00:04:46,126 --> 00:04:49,526
[Not Today Reporter, Kwon Tae Seong]

73
00:04:56,290 --> 00:04:58,892
[Gate 3]

74
00:05:00,059 --> 00:05:01,599
[Emergency Stairs]

75
00:05:01,599 --> 00:05:02,999
Ms. Yoo.

76
00:05:02,999 --> 00:05:06,415
About ten minutes ago,
two men ran in through Gate 3.

77
00:05:06,415 --> 00:05:08,915
It looked like they were chasing each other.

78
00:05:08,915 --> 00:05:11,755
They went into the emergency stairwell
one after another.

79
00:05:11,755 --> 00:05:15,226
Five minutes later,
only the first man came back out.

80
00:05:16,339 --> 00:05:18,135
I missed them.

81
00:05:18,135 --> 00:05:19,327
I'm sorry, Ms. Yoo.

82
00:05:19,327 --> 00:05:22,551
Okay. Keep watching.

83
00:05:22,551 --> 00:05:24,251
But what...

84
00:05:27,363 --> 00:05:29,526
You should be more careful.

85
00:05:35,292 --> 00:05:37,092
[Emergency Call]

86
00:05:38,363 --> 00:05:41,279
Yes, someone has collapsed and is bleeding
from the head on the fifth floor

87
00:05:41,279 --> 00:05:43,635
of the emergency stairs at King Tower.

88
00:05:43,635 --> 00:05:45,859
I think he's going to die
if you don't get here quickly.

89
00:06:01,275 --> 00:06:02,659
Try to stay alive if you can.

90
00:06:02,659 --> 00:06:05,147
Looks like they won the soccer game too.

91
00:06:05,147 --> 00:06:07,592
One victim is enough for today.

92
00:06:13,959 --> 00:06:16,226
[Four Months Later]

93
00:06:16,226 --> 00:06:17,226
[Kwon Tae Seong]
Let me see.

94
00:06:17,226 --> 00:06:18,635
Ugh, what?

95
00:06:18,635 --> 00:06:19,735
Hold still.

96
00:06:19,735 --> 00:06:20,987
- Wait, what is it?
- Let me see.

97
00:06:20,987 --> 00:06:23,592
Oh, come on. What is it?

98
00:06:27,119 --> 00:06:28,827
Looks like your head's still attached.

99
00:06:28,827 --> 00:06:30,926
Are you insane?

100
00:06:31,675 --> 00:06:34,839
Oh, right, I can walk starting today.

101
00:06:34,839 --> 00:06:36,959
Hey, hey, hey! Hey!

102
00:06:39,392 --> 00:06:40,392
It feels weird.

103
00:06:40,392 --> 00:06:42,527
If you saw a pickpocket,
you should've called the police.

104
00:06:42,527 --> 00:06:44,126
Why did you chase him, you punk?

105
00:06:44,126 --> 00:06:46,459
I think I've got a cramp.

106
00:06:47,307 --> 00:06:49,663
How do you give me the same lecture
every time you visit?

107
00:06:49,663 --> 00:06:50,939
Impressive, really.

108
00:06:50,939 --> 00:06:54,051
Ugh, I've heard it enough already.

109
00:06:54,051 --> 00:06:55,971
You think this is funny?
You feel like laughing right now?

110
00:06:55,971 --> 00:06:58,407
You just woke up after four months,
you crazy punk.

111
00:06:58,407 --> 00:07:01,326
How could you call someone
with a head injury "crazy"?

112
00:07:04,251 --> 00:07:05,351
Oh, right!

113
00:07:05,351 --> 00:07:07,171
You still haven't caught the guy
who hit me from behind, right?

114
00:07:07,171 --> 00:07:09,727
Don't go trying to catch him yourself.

115
00:07:09,727 --> 00:07:11,191
Why?

116
00:07:11,191 --> 00:07:12,855
Because I think you'd actually kill him
if you caught him.

117
00:07:12,855 --> 00:07:14,219
Of course, I would. Completely.

118
00:07:14,219 --> 00:07:15,926
You really...

119
00:07:19,123 --> 00:07:20,963
Hey!

120
00:07:20,963 --> 00:07:22,719
Did you even know the rooftop

121
00:07:22,719 --> 00:07:25,003
where you collapsed
was the Kingfisher sniper's position?

122
00:07:25,003 --> 00:07:27,719
Exactly. Oh! What a darn waste.

123
00:07:27,719 --> 00:07:31,207
If I hadn't cracked my head,
I could've met Kingfisher.

124
00:07:31,207 --> 00:07:32,755
You probably would've.

125
00:07:32,755 --> 00:07:36,051
Instead, you would've had
a hole in your head, you punk.

126
00:07:36,051 --> 00:07:38,359
That's defamatory toward Kingfisher.

127
00:07:38,359 --> 00:07:41,826
Why? Because I'm an innocent citizen.

128
00:07:43,071 --> 00:07:46,671
I can't tell if you are lucky or unlucky...

129
00:07:46,671 --> 00:07:50,292
I'm really anxious about
what kind of woman will take you away.

130
00:08:13,331 --> 00:08:16,131
Manager Yoo, you don't have to
come by so often. I feel bad about it.

131
00:08:16,131 --> 00:08:18,347
It's not like being sick
is anything to brag about.

132
00:08:18,347 --> 00:08:20,726
You got hurt doing your job.

133
00:08:21,503 --> 00:08:23,007
How are you feeling?

134
00:08:23,007 --> 00:08:26,847
Maybe it's because I'm getting older.
Even my bones aren't healing properly.

135
00:08:26,847 --> 00:08:29,483
Oh, you've all been through a lot
because of me, right?

136
00:08:29,483 --> 00:08:31,555
Everyone's worried about you.

137
00:08:31,555 --> 00:08:34,339
You know you need to be careful about
complications after a traffic accident?

138
00:08:34,339 --> 00:08:36,326
Then this...

139
00:08:37,163 --> 00:08:38,691
Darn it.

140
00:08:38,691 --> 00:08:40,391
This is good.

141
00:08:46,399 --> 00:08:48,459
- This?
- Yeah.

142
00:08:55,255 --> 00:08:57,003
Oh, by the way,

143
00:08:57,003 --> 00:08:59,526
I hear the rookie is pretty capable.

144
00:08:59,526 --> 00:09:01,943
Yeah, after Assistant Manager Son quit,

145
00:09:01,943 --> 00:09:04,659
I was worried about
how to fill such a big vacancy.

146
00:09:04,659 --> 00:09:07,979
But now I can breathe easier.

147
00:09:07,979 --> 00:09:09,955
The vacancy you left
is even bigger, Director.

148
00:09:09,955 --> 00:09:11,883
Please get well and come back soon.

149
00:09:11,883 --> 00:09:15,626
I can't leave in peace until you're back.

150
00:09:17,395 --> 00:09:20,527
Manager Yoo, have you made up your mind?

151
00:09:20,527 --> 00:09:24,027
Are you really going to quit?

152
00:09:24,027 --> 00:09:26,126
I think I'm just tired.

153
00:09:26,126 --> 00:09:28,435
Yeah. I can understand that.

154
00:09:28,435 --> 00:09:34,231
They say even ordinary people
can burn out after working for ten years.

155
00:09:34,231 --> 00:09:39,383
You've been working nonstop.
No wonder you're exhausted.

156
00:09:39,383 --> 00:09:41,083
Right?

157
00:09:42,487 --> 00:09:45,559
And this isn't exactly
an ordinary line of work, right?

158
00:09:45,559 --> 00:09:49,203
It's endless, no matter how much you do.

159
00:09:49,203 --> 00:09:52,267
And the world stays exactly the same.

160
00:09:52,267 --> 00:09:56,559
I understand how you feel.

161
00:09:56,559 --> 00:09:58,292
Manager Yoo.

162
00:09:59,007 --> 00:10:01,519
Could you reconsider it one more time?

163
00:10:01,519 --> 00:10:04,692
For now, stay off on-site meetings.

164
00:10:04,692 --> 00:10:09,003
Just take it easy, okay?

165
00:10:30,391 --> 00:10:34,926
[10 Lifestyle Tips for Cancer Prevention]

166
00:10:49,960 --> 00:10:51,660
Just a moment!

167
00:10:54,331 --> 00:10:56,292
Come down. Hurry.

168
00:11:00,907 --> 00:11:03,259
Come on, slow down!

169
00:11:04,687 --> 00:11:06,971
Why?

170
00:11:06,971 --> 00:11:10,443
Huh? "Why?"

171
00:11:10,443 --> 00:11:12,143
Oh, why...

172
00:11:13,440 --> 00:11:15,492
Because life is precious?

173
00:11:16,647 --> 00:11:18,726
What I'm trying to say is,

174
00:11:18,726 --> 00:11:21,792
after nearly dying recently,
I realized a few things.

175
00:11:21,792 --> 00:11:23,471
I mean...

176
00:11:23,471 --> 00:11:27,492
Just looking at the sky,
watching the leaves change.

177
00:11:27,492 --> 00:11:29,726
"Wow, I'm glad I'm alive."

178
00:11:30,444 --> 00:11:32,626
"It's good to be alive."

179
00:11:32,626 --> 00:11:37,827
Joking around with friends,
getting nagged by your family...

180
00:11:37,827 --> 00:11:39,295
Worrying about silly things like,

181
00:11:39,295 --> 00:11:41,848
"What should I eat today?"
or "What should I wear tomorrow?"

182
00:11:41,848 --> 00:11:46,192
That ordinary everyday life is so precious.
It really is precious.

183
00:11:46,192 --> 00:11:47,959
So...

184
00:11:50,555 --> 00:11:53,726
I hope you live and don't die.

185
00:12:31,352 --> 00:12:33,746
Says life is precious,
yet here you are smoking,

186
00:12:33,746 --> 00:12:35,326
especially after you nearly died?

187
00:12:35,326 --> 00:12:36,671
Isn't that a little much?

188
00:12:36,671 --> 00:12:39,626
This isn't mine.
I just found it on my way here...

189
00:12:42,399 --> 00:12:43,921
Take care.

190
00:12:43,921 --> 00:12:46,592
Enjoy your ordinary life, one day at a time.

191
00:12:47,447 --> 00:12:49,226
Excuse me!

192
00:12:51,626 --> 00:12:54,326
Have we met before?

193
00:12:57,515 --> 00:12:58,831
No.

194
00:12:58,831 --> 00:13:00,625
I'm sure I've seen you before.

195
00:13:00,625 --> 00:13:02,659
Even your voice sounds familiar.

196
00:13:04,505 --> 00:13:07,454
Oh, I'm sorry. I...

197
00:13:07,454 --> 00:13:11,187
I injured my head,
so I think I'm a little out of it.

198
00:13:11,187 --> 00:13:15,326
I'm sure my memory will come back
once I fully recover, right?

199
00:13:16,763 --> 00:13:18,192
<i>"Kwon Tae Seong."</i>

200
00:13:18,192 --> 00:13:19,959
[Not Today Social Affairs Reporter]
He works for an online news outlet.

201
00:13:19,959 --> 00:13:22,927
I looked through some of his past articles.

202
00:13:22,927 --> 00:13:24,051
[Supporting the vulnerable]
His focus is on social justice

203
00:13:24,051 --> 00:13:25,451
[isn't a privilege, but a choice]
and protecting the vulnerable.

204
00:13:25,451 --> 00:13:27,408
He's a pretty rare type
of reporter these days.

205
00:13:27,408 --> 00:13:29,599
But why him?

206
00:13:29,599 --> 00:13:31,763
Just in case, for precaution. Keep going.

207
00:13:31,763 --> 00:13:33,459
Is this why you're interested in him?

208
00:13:33,459 --> 00:13:34,526
[Kingfisher]

209
00:13:34,526 --> 00:13:38,659
Every article about Kingfisher
in this outlet was written by him.

210
00:13:38,659 --> 00:13:40,564
I skimmed through them.

211
00:13:40,564 --> 00:13:41,728
He doesn't really

212
00:13:41,728 --> 00:13:43,151
[Kingfisher: Notorious Killer]
take a negative stance on Kingfisher.

213
00:13:43,151 --> 00:13:44,154
[or Avenger of Justice?]
He's more focused on

214
00:13:44,154 --> 00:13:45,715
analyzing the phenomenon
than just following the cases.

215
00:13:45,715 --> 00:13:50,159
Apparently, both the industry and readers
consider his articles fairly insightful.

216
00:13:50,159 --> 00:13:53,859
Oh, and he has a personal blog too.

217
00:13:53,859 --> 00:13:56,539
Send me the link,
along with the article right now.

218
00:13:56,539 --> 00:13:58,239
All of it?

219
00:13:59,992 --> 00:14:03,926
She normally doesn't even
care about the articles...

220
00:14:10,575 --> 00:14:13,610
<i>"Kingfisher: Notorious Killer
or Avenger of Justice?"</i>

221
00:14:13,610 --> 00:14:15,160
<i>"The Painful Questions Kingfisher
Forces Our Society to Ask."</i>

222
00:14:15,160 --> 00:14:17,087
<i>"Five Reflections on Kingfisher."</i>

223
00:14:17,087 --> 00:14:19,879
<i>"Can We Really Trust Our Justice System?"</i>

224
00:14:19,879 --> 00:14:22,692
<i>"If I Ever Meet Kingfisher."</i>

225
00:14:22,692 --> 00:14:26,434
<i>Luckily, I grew up smoothly
in the care of a close-knit family,</i>

226
00:14:26,434 --> 00:14:30,295
<i>and I was a pretty ordinary,
well-behaved student throughout school.</i>

227
00:14:30,295 --> 00:14:32,467
How about best of three?
Loser pays for the pizza.

228
00:14:32,467 --> 00:14:34,927
Don't be a sore loser if you lose, huh?

229
00:14:34,927 --> 00:14:36,727
You'd better not lose
and start crying, you punk.

230
00:14:36,727 --> 00:14:38,359
Hey, how many times have you lost already?

231
00:14:38,359 --> 00:14:40,159
Oh, forget it.

232
00:14:59,099 --> 00:15:02,375
<i>If it weren't for a tragic incident
that happened to a friend one day,</i>

233
00:15:02,375 --> 00:15:06,819
<i>I might have lived a life
distant from crime and illegality.</i>

234
00:15:06,819 --> 00:15:11,291
<i>A sniper shooting occurred
in the heart of Seoul.</i>

235
00:15:11,291 --> 00:15:12,291
<i>According to police,</i>

236
00:15:12,291 --> 00:15:13,292
- <i>at an officetel in Semyung-dong,</i>
- A gun?

237
00:15:13,292 --> 00:15:15,603
- <i>a man in his 40s was shot...</i>
- Look at that.

238
00:15:15,603 --> 00:15:19,523
<i>I still remember the shock
of first hearing about him.</i>

239
00:15:19,523 --> 00:15:22,326
<i>Someone out there picks out
only the cruel, ruthless criminals</i>

240
00:15:22,326 --> 00:15:25,467
<i>who crush the everyday lives
of decent people and eliminates them?</i>

241
00:15:25,467 --> 00:15:28,658
Honestly, isn't Kingfisher kind of cool?

242
00:15:28,658 --> 00:15:30,723
What's cool about him?
He's just a psycho killer.

243
00:15:30,723 --> 00:15:33,724
Hey, but he only picks
and kills the bad guys.

244
00:15:33,724 --> 00:15:38,459
Even if he only kills bad people,
a killer is still a killer.

245
00:15:38,459 --> 00:15:43,417
<i>While the world was divided in its opinions,
I couldn't help wondering.</i>

246
00:15:43,417 --> 00:15:45,059
<i>What kind of person</i>

247
00:15:45,059 --> 00:15:48,359
<i>would devote their entire life
to something like that?</i>

248
00:15:55,259 --> 00:15:57,042
[Reporter Attacked While Covering Pickpockets
Wakes Up After Four Months]

249
00:15:57,042 --> 00:15:58,394
Reporter Kwon, on the day of the incident...

250
00:15:59,592 --> 00:16:02,525
[Rooftop Where Reporter Kwon Collapsed
Revealed as Kingfisher's Sniper's Nest]

251
00:16:31,963 --> 00:16:33,931
<i>Have we met before?</i>

252
00:16:33,931 --> 00:16:38,359
I'm sure my memory will come back
once I fully recover, right?

253
00:17:00,963 --> 00:17:02,211
I don't think you made this yourself.

254
00:17:02,211 --> 00:17:03,211
I made it myself.

255
00:17:03,211 --> 00:17:06,192
- You bought this?
- No, I made it.

256
00:17:07,139 --> 00:17:08,139
How is it?

257
00:17:08,139 --> 00:17:10,307
- You bought this?
- No, it's not!

258
00:17:10,307 --> 00:17:12,407
I really made it. I really did.

259
00:17:12,407 --> 00:17:14,459
I really made it.

260
00:17:16,231 --> 00:17:18,467
How is it?

261
00:17:18,467 --> 00:17:19,539
It's good.

262
00:17:19,539 --> 00:17:21,059
Is that it?

263
00:17:21,059 --> 00:17:23,092
What more do you want? I said it's good.

264
00:17:23,092 --> 00:17:25,626
I made it, and I did a good job.

265
00:17:30,139 --> 00:17:32,126
Miss! Excuse me, just a moment!

266
00:17:32,851 --> 00:17:35,459
Wow, I finally found you.

267
00:17:35,459 --> 00:17:38,031
I've been waiting for you.

268
00:17:38,031 --> 00:17:39,626
Why?

269
00:17:39,626 --> 00:17:42,659
I remembered where we met.

270
00:17:44,811 --> 00:17:46,992
You lived in Hoewon-dong
when you were little, right?

271
00:17:48,595 --> 00:17:50,626
No, I've never lived there.

272
00:17:52,783 --> 00:17:54,795
You went to Jeongin Middle School, right?

273
00:17:54,795 --> 00:17:56,495
No.

274
00:17:58,959 --> 00:18:00,223
Did you ever attend Bright Shine Academy...

275
00:18:00,223 --> 00:18:01,923
No.

276
00:18:05,435 --> 00:18:08,691
Has anyone ever told you that
you look like actress Choi So Hyun...

277
00:18:08,691 --> 00:18:11,015
No, right?

278
00:18:12,255 --> 00:18:13,447
I'm sorry.

279
00:18:13,447 --> 00:18:17,019
I'll think harder

280
00:18:17,019 --> 00:18:20,726
and try to figure it out next time.

281
00:18:27,147 --> 00:18:31,291
Oh, you might think
I'm trying to hit on you or something,

282
00:18:31,291 --> 00:18:33,007
but I'm absolutely not. Absolutely not.

283
00:18:33,007 --> 00:18:34,826
If we happen to run into each other again...

284
00:18:34,826 --> 00:18:36,795
No, that won't happen.

285
00:18:36,795 --> 00:18:39,339
Don't waste your time.

286
00:18:39,339 --> 00:18:41,679
We've never met.

287
00:18:41,679 --> 00:18:43,379
Wait...

288
00:18:45,375 --> 00:18:47,192
She's got no mercy.

289
00:18:49,383 --> 00:18:52,159
Oh, I should have asked her name.

290
00:19:00,471 --> 00:19:02,131
<i>Are you having trouble sleeping?</i>

291
00:19:02,131 --> 00:19:03,699
<i>Even when you fall asleep, you wake up soon,</i>

292
00:19:03,699 --> 00:19:05,892
and you sometimes have nightmares, right?

293
00:19:05,892 --> 00:19:06,927
Yeah, well...

294
00:19:06,927 --> 00:19:10,492
Have you experienced
any major stress recently?

295
00:19:14,723 --> 00:19:19,692
Problems in your relationships,
or pressure at work?

296
00:19:22,426 --> 00:19:24,226
No, nothing.

297
00:19:24,226 --> 00:19:26,448
Still nothing, huh?

298
00:19:26,448 --> 00:19:27,731
All right.

299
00:19:27,731 --> 00:19:31,235
I can increase the dosage
of your sleeping pills,

300
00:19:31,235 --> 00:19:32,935
but I think...

301
00:19:39,191 --> 00:19:42,892
You're pretty good. Is it fun?

302
00:19:48,903 --> 00:19:50,111
Oh, really?

303
00:19:50,111 --> 00:19:51,659
Want to go watch it later?

304
00:19:51,659 --> 00:19:53,492
- No, we can't.
- Ah.

305
00:19:53,492 --> 00:19:56,359
No, here it is!

306
00:20:01,392 --> 00:20:04,699
[Sales Team 3 Team Leader, Bae Yun Ok]

307
00:20:04,699 --> 00:20:07,079
[Resignation Letter]
I hereby resign.

308
00:20:07,079 --> 00:20:09,426
Please accept my resignation,
Team Leader Bae.

309
00:20:35,495 --> 00:20:38,059
Here they come. Here they come.

310
00:20:38,059 --> 00:20:40,067
Here they come!

311
00:20:40,067 --> 00:20:42,375
Have you figured out how the two men
ended up getting hit by the same shot?

312
00:20:42,375 --> 00:20:44,592
Could the target have been only one person,
with Kingfisher accidentally...

313
00:20:44,592 --> 00:20:46,667
We're not cops.
We're just employees out for a meal.

314
00:20:46,667 --> 00:20:47,667
- Yeah.
- He says he's not a cop.

315
00:20:47,667 --> 00:20:50,126
- He's not a cop?
- What?

316
00:20:52,959 --> 00:20:54,279
You're a pretty good liar, aren't you?

317
00:20:54,279 --> 00:20:56,431
Hey, half of it was true.

318
00:20:56,431 --> 00:20:58,359
It's true we're not the local police here.

319
00:20:58,359 --> 00:21:00,047
I'm so hungry I'm about to pass out.

320
00:21:00,047 --> 00:21:02,163
All I ate last night was two chocolate pies.

321
00:21:02,163 --> 00:21:04,095
I had one cream bun.

322
00:21:04,095 --> 00:21:05,795
Oh...

323
00:21:06,451 --> 00:21:10,579
Wow, looks like the one-shot double kill
really is the hottest topic.

324
00:21:10,579 --> 00:21:13,087
It's the first case like this in 16 years.

325
00:21:13,087 --> 00:21:15,139
And the internet is going crazy over it.

326
00:21:15,139 --> 00:21:16,951
The original target was just Tak Jong Gu.

327
00:21:16,951 --> 00:21:18,975
Kingfisher was trying to shoot him
and accidentally killed someone else.

328
00:21:18,975 --> 00:21:22,192
Do you really think Kingfisher is
the kind of guy who'd make a mistake?

329
00:21:22,192 --> 00:21:23,947
No way. He'd never do that!

330
00:21:23,947 --> 00:21:26,199
Anyway, let's say Tak Jong Gu is one thing,

331
00:21:26,199 --> 00:21:28,947
but that Cheon... whatever his name is,
what's the chairman's charge?

332
00:21:28,947 --> 00:21:30,819
That's what we're about to find out.

333
00:21:30,819 --> 00:21:33,799
Why Cheon Seong Gil became a target.

334
00:21:33,799 --> 00:21:36,439
Right now? Without even eating first?

335
00:21:36,439 --> 00:21:39,455
Sir, I only had two chocolate pies... Sir!

336
00:21:39,455 --> 00:21:42,947
<i>This case is unusual not only
because there are two victims,</i>

337
00:21:42,947 --> 00:21:47,139
<i>but also because the criminal history
of one of them hasn't been confirmed yet.</i>

338
00:21:47,139 --> 00:21:49,420
<i>So, the question is whether Kingfisher</i>

339
00:21:49,420 --> 00:21:51,926
<i>may have accidentally killed
an innocent person...</i>

340
00:21:51,926 --> 00:21:55,475
<i>If that turns out to be true,
public opinion could shift dramatically.</i>

341
00:21:55,475 --> 00:21:58,275
<i>Until now, he was believed
to only kill serious criminals...</i>

342
00:21:58,275 --> 00:21:59,275
Yes, Ms. Gu.

343
00:21:59,275 --> 00:22:00,927
[Reporter Gu Hae Na]
<i>Mr. Kwon, where are you now?</i>

344
00:22:00,927 --> 00:22:02,819
We've heard from someone
with information on Cheon Seong Gil.

345
00:22:02,819 --> 00:22:04,855
They've agreed to an interview.

346
00:22:04,855 --> 00:22:07,292
<i>We're meeting them right now.</i>

347
00:22:08,215 --> 00:22:09,879
<i>Hello?</i>

348
00:22:09,879 --> 00:22:13,547
Mr. Kwon? Are you listening?

349
00:22:13,547 --> 00:22:15,792
Where are you meeting them?

350
00:22:21,935 --> 00:22:23,526
Mother, I'm here.

351
00:22:23,526 --> 00:22:24,871
Oh, welcome...

352
00:22:24,871 --> 00:22:27,731
Bo Na, what brings you here at this hour?
Didn't you go to work?

353
00:22:27,731 --> 00:22:31,247
Well, my business trip ended a day early,
so I don't have to go in today.

354
00:22:31,247 --> 00:22:34,523
And I brought something for you, Mother.

355
00:22:34,523 --> 00:22:37,692
Huh? What is it?

356
00:22:38,691 --> 00:22:41,231
I thought you might be
having trouble sleeping lately

357
00:22:41,231 --> 00:22:44,047
and getting hot flashes, so I was worried.

358
00:22:44,047 --> 00:22:47,691
I've indeed been a bit hot
under the collar lately.

359
00:22:47,691 --> 00:22:50,527
But I wonder why that is?

360
00:22:50,527 --> 00:22:53,171
Mother, they say
that's all part of menopause.

361
00:22:53,171 --> 00:22:55,992
But if you take one packet a day,
it helps manage...

362
00:22:55,992 --> 00:22:58,123
Oh, jeez.

363
00:22:58,123 --> 00:23:00,126
Well, is there anything I can help with?

364
00:23:00,126 --> 00:23:01,571
What could you possibly help with?

365
00:23:01,571 --> 00:23:03,679
You must be tired from your business trip.
Go home and get some rest.

366
00:23:03,679 --> 00:23:05,443
No, I'm fine.

367
00:23:05,443 --> 00:23:07,215
It's not like anyone's provoking me.

368
00:23:07,215 --> 00:23:09,711
Hey, if you have eyes, just look around.

369
00:23:09,711 --> 00:23:11,687
Do you see anything that needs helping with?

370
00:23:11,687 --> 00:23:13,055
Oh, dear.

371
00:23:13,055 --> 00:23:15,027
Even if there were something to do,

372
00:23:15,027 --> 00:23:17,039
would I feel comfortable asking you to do it?

373
00:23:17,039 --> 00:23:20,015
If I push my precious
daughter-in-law too hard,

374
00:23:20,015 --> 00:23:23,287
I'll get an earful from my son again.

375
00:23:23,287 --> 00:23:26,667
Mom, why are you taking it out on her?

376
00:23:26,667 --> 00:23:29,759
She's just cranky because business is slow.

377
00:23:30,726 --> 00:23:31,851
Mother.

378
00:23:31,851 --> 00:23:35,055
This can help with mood swings
during menopause too!

379
00:23:35,055 --> 00:23:36,922
Yeah, Mom. Want me to open it for you?

380
00:23:36,922 --> 00:23:39,155
What...

381
00:23:39,155 --> 00:23:41,359
Oh, welcome!

382
00:23:42,426 --> 00:23:45,339
- Hello.
- Oh, my, welcome.

383
00:23:45,339 --> 00:23:47,007
- Have a seat here.
- Welcome.

384
00:23:47,007 --> 00:23:48,859
Oh, Mr. Kim, what brings you here?

385
00:23:48,859 --> 00:23:52,395
I came by for lunch after the neighborhood
merchant association meeting.

386
00:23:52,395 --> 00:23:54,171
Oh, my, thank you.

387
00:23:54,171 --> 00:23:56,995
About twenty more people
will be coming later.

388
00:23:56,995 --> 00:24:00,992
The director of the senior center next door
was looking for a good chicken shop,

389
00:24:00,992 --> 00:24:02,719
so I recommended yours.

390
00:24:02,719 --> 00:24:04,931
Oh, my goodness.

391
00:24:04,931 --> 00:24:07,743
Oh, my, Mr. Kim, you're such a lifesaver.

392
00:24:07,743 --> 00:24:09,026
Just give us a moment.

393
00:24:09,026 --> 00:24:11,826
- We'll make it delicious.
- Everyone, please order.

394
00:24:13,615 --> 00:24:16,326
Hello, this is Tae Seong Chicken.

395
00:24:16,326 --> 00:24:18,235
Pardon? The children's welfare center?

396
00:24:18,235 --> 00:24:20,135
Yes, I know it.

397
00:24:20,135 --> 00:24:21,455
Yes.

398
00:24:21,455 --> 00:24:23,711
What? Twenty chickens?

399
00:24:23,711 --> 00:24:25,719
By five o'clock?

400
00:24:25,719 --> 00:24:28,751
Yes, we'll make them deliciously
and send them over.

401
00:24:28,751 --> 00:24:30,099
Okay.

402
00:24:30,099 --> 00:24:31,427
Twenty chickens?

403
00:24:31,427 --> 00:24:33,211
- Yeah.
- What's going on?

404
00:24:33,211 --> 00:24:35,255
What do you mean, "what's going on"?
It's a lucky day.

405
00:24:35,255 --> 00:24:37,747
- Start frying the chicken.
- Got it.

406
00:24:37,747 --> 00:24:41,079
We're in trouble.
We've got our hands full now.

407
00:24:41,079 --> 00:24:42,779
I'm right here...

408
00:24:43,503 --> 00:24:46,459
Yul's mommy, are you still here?

409
00:24:47,219 --> 00:24:49,159
Mother, I'm here.

410
00:24:50,059 --> 00:24:51,183
Thank you.

411
00:24:51,183 --> 00:24:52,903
- Take care going home. Alright.
- Thank you!

412
00:24:52,903 --> 00:24:54,626
Take care.

413
00:24:59,615 --> 00:25:01,779
This worked out perfectly, didn't it?

414
00:25:01,779 --> 00:25:04,759
I wondered how we could write a story
without any witnesses or evidence.

415
00:25:04,759 --> 00:25:07,579
It couldn't have been easy,
but they found the courage to come forward.

416
00:25:07,579 --> 00:25:10,892
Jeez, what, innocent lives?

417
00:25:10,892 --> 00:25:14,359
They have no idea
how evil Cheon Seong Gil was.

418
00:25:14,975 --> 00:25:16,675
Let's go.

419
00:25:19,439 --> 00:25:22,691
But, Mr. Kwon, your intuition is amazing.

420
00:25:22,691 --> 00:25:24,899
Like with Pyo Kyu Cheol last time,

421
00:25:24,899 --> 00:25:29,231
how do you keep picking out exactly
the people Kingfisher targets?

422
00:25:29,231 --> 00:25:34,955
At this rate, aren't we going to
run into Kingfisher somewhere?

423
00:25:34,955 --> 00:25:38,392
Maybe we've already crossed paths
without even knowing it, right?

424
00:25:39,019 --> 00:25:42,415
Aren't you scared? Who knows
what will happen once Kingfisher shows up?

425
00:25:42,415 --> 00:25:43,603
What?

426
00:25:43,603 --> 00:25:48,775
Oh, come on. I'm just an innocent citizen.

427
00:25:48,775 --> 00:25:50,475
Let's go, Mr. Kwon.

428
00:25:53,475 --> 00:25:55,092
It's hot, so be careful.

429
00:25:55,092 --> 00:25:56,527
- Ma'am, one more fried chicken, please.
- Yes.

430
00:25:56,527 --> 00:25:58,903
Okay, one fried chicken.
Sun Il, one more fried chicken!

431
00:25:58,903 --> 00:26:00,123
- Oh, got it.
- Yeah.

432
00:26:00,123 --> 00:26:01,679
- And one Coke, please.
- Want a Coke?

433
00:26:01,679 --> 00:26:02,867
Oh, I'll get it.

434
00:26:02,867 --> 00:26:05,487
- Take these to the empty tables.
- Yeah, Mother.

435
00:26:05,487 --> 00:26:06,771
Want some more pickled radish?

436
00:26:06,771 --> 00:26:08,351
Here, your Coke.

437
00:26:08,351 --> 00:26:09,919
Want more sauce?

438
00:26:09,919 --> 00:26:10,992
The drumstick is mine.

439
00:26:10,992 --> 00:26:13,192
I'll give you a cider on the house.

440
00:26:13,192 --> 00:26:14,463
[Mr. Kim Gil Dong,
Real Estate Business Owner]

441
00:26:14,463 --> 00:26:17,547
<i>We'll make good use of the donation
you sent to the merchants' association.</i>

442
00:26:17,547 --> 00:26:19,632
[Tae Seong Chicken]
<i>It would have been great to publicize it</i>

443
00:26:19,632 --> 00:26:21,447
<i>as a win-win effort with our tenants,</i>

444
00:26:21,447 --> 00:26:23,759
<i>but since you asked
to remain anonymous, that's a shame.</i>

445
00:26:23,759 --> 00:26:25,811
[Jung Kyung Hwa]
<i>Thank you for the chicken.</i>

446
00:26:25,811 --> 00:26:27,947
[Director of the Child Welfare Center]
<i>The kids are so excited and waiting for it.</i>

447
00:26:27,947 --> 00:26:29,595
<i>We'll enjoy it.</i>

448
00:26:29,595 --> 00:26:31,295
Thank you.

449
00:26:38,031 --> 00:26:41,283
<i>Attention is once again
turning to Chairman Cheon,</i>

450
00:26:41,283 --> 00:26:44,259
<i>who was killed in the shooting
at the casino VIP lounge.</i>

451
00:26:44,259 --> 00:26:47,674
<i>Chairman Cheon, known as
Kingfisher's first civilian victim,</i>

452
00:26:47,674 --> 00:26:48,674
<i>was a respected businessman</i>

453
00:26:48,674 --> 00:26:49,674
[Chairman Cheon]
<i>who made significant contributions</i>

454
00:26:49,674 --> 00:26:51,495
[Renowned Businessman in Gangwon Province]
<i>to Gangwon Province's economy.</i>

455
00:26:51,495 --> 00:26:54,392
- <i>Following Kingfisher's sniper attack...</i>
- I knew it would happen someday.

456
00:26:54,392 --> 00:26:57,687
He was acting all high and mighty,
like a hero or something.

457
00:26:57,687 --> 00:27:00,519
If an innocent person was killed,
he should be held accountable too.

458
00:27:00,519 --> 00:27:02,251
Kingfisher should be caught
and locked up too.

459
00:27:02,251 --> 00:27:04,559
I'll give you the sauced one.
Sun Il, one more sauced chicken here!

460
00:27:04,559 --> 00:27:05,559
- Oh, one sauced chicken.
- Ma'am.

461
00:27:05,559 --> 00:27:06,691
- Yes?
- When will the fried chicken be ready?

462
00:27:06,691 --> 00:27:08,059
The fried chicken?
Sun Il, when is the fried chicken coming out?

463
00:27:08,059 --> 00:27:10,039
- It's out now!
- I'll bring it right out.

464
00:27:10,039 --> 00:27:12,359
<i>Along with the exact circumstances
of Chairman Cheon's death,</i>

465
00:27:12,359 --> 00:27:15,299
<i>the police are also expanding their
investigation into Kingfisher's motives.</i>

466
00:27:15,299 --> 00:27:18,307
What do these people take our Kingfisher for?

467
00:27:18,307 --> 00:27:21,759
What do we do? Director Yoo's going to be
so upset when she hears about this.

468
00:27:21,759 --> 00:27:23,626
Of course, she will.

469
00:27:23,626 --> 00:27:28,292
It's the most important principle
Director Yoo has upheld for 16 years.

470
00:27:28,292 --> 00:27:29,992
[Kingfisher Mistake Controversy,
First Innocent Civilian Sniper Attack?]

471
00:27:34,859 --> 00:27:37,003
I got a text from Director Yoo.

472
00:27:37,003 --> 00:27:38,159
What did she say?

473
00:27:38,159 --> 00:27:39,707
[Reliable Police, A Safe Country]

474
00:27:39,707 --> 00:27:42,559
Hey, get reporters out of the doorway.

475
00:27:43,843 --> 00:27:48,711
Why does that Kingfisher punk
have to come all the way out here...

476
00:27:48,711 --> 00:27:50,411
and cause trouble?

477
00:27:52,659 --> 00:27:54,924
Oh, my, since earlier,

478
00:27:54,924 --> 00:27:56,503
[The Kingfisher Casino Case]
what case have you been digging into?

479
00:27:56,503 --> 00:27:59,507
I heard you went to the scene.

480
00:27:59,507 --> 00:28:04,631
It was obvious the two targets
just happened to be in the same place...

481
00:28:04,631 --> 00:28:06,543
Chairman Cheon has a criminal record.

482
00:28:06,543 --> 00:28:08,907
The sexual assault charge?

483
00:28:08,907 --> 00:28:11,983
Oh, that was a long time ago.

484
00:28:11,983 --> 00:28:15,495
What about those workers who died
at his construction site recently?

485
00:28:15,495 --> 00:28:20,951
Those cases were already closed
as accidental falls and suicides.

486
00:28:20,951 --> 00:28:23,207
Reporters came looking into them too,

487
00:28:23,207 --> 00:28:26,259
but there was nothing to find,
so nothing ever came of it.

488
00:28:29,692 --> 00:28:30,692
<i>Breaking news.</i>

489
00:28:30,692 --> 00:28:32,142
[Kingfisher Casino Case Victim]
<i>The full extent of the hidden crimes</i>

490
00:28:32,142 --> 00:28:33,592
[Chairman Cheon's Crimes Revealed]
<i>of Chairman Cheon,</i>

491
00:28:33,592 --> 00:28:36,199
- <i>the casino case victim, once known as</i>
- Sir, look at that!

492
00:28:36,199 --> 00:28:39,072
- <i>Kingfisher's first civilian victim,</i>
- Huh? Turn it up a bit.

493
00:28:39,072 --> 00:28:40,251
<i>has now been revealed.</i>

494
00:28:40,251 --> 00:28:44,555
<i>Chairman Cheon repeatedly sexually assaulted
the wife of a construction worker</i>

495
00:28:44,555 --> 00:28:46,291
<i>after hiring her as a housekeeper.</i>

496
00:28:46,291 --> 00:28:48,167
- <i>When her husband found out</i>
- Oh, my!

497
00:28:48,167 --> 00:28:49,859
<i>and threatened to report him to the police,</i>

498
00:28:49,859 --> 00:28:53,275
<i>Cheon bribed a fellow worker with money
and had the husband murdered</i>

499
00:28:53,275 --> 00:28:54,371
- <i>through contract killing.</i>
- That, that...

500
00:28:54,371 --> 00:28:56,431
- <i>These facts were revealed directly</i>
- What is that?

501
00:28:56,431 --> 00:28:57,792
<i>by the wife of the murdered worker.</i>

502
00:28:57,792 --> 00:29:02,059
<i>This is expected to put to rest claims
that Kingfisher had killed</i>

503
00:29:02,059 --> 00:29:04,003
[Chairman Cheon, Kingfisher Target,]
<i>an innocent civilian for the first time.</i>

504
00:29:04,003 --> 00:29:05,599
[Accused of Sexual Assault, Murder-for-Hire]
<i>Police are verifying the report</i>

505
00:29:05,599 --> 00:29:07,627
[Investigative Reporting Team Reporter]
<i>while launching an internal investigation</i>

506
00:29:07,627 --> 00:29:10,859
[Gu Hae Na]
<i>into additional criminal allegations</i>

507
00:29:10,859 --> 00:29:12,392
- <i>involving Chairman Cheon.</i>
- Gu Hae Na!

508
00:29:12,392 --> 00:29:13,695
<i>In our broadcast, Kingfisher...</i>

509
00:29:13,695 --> 00:29:16,811
Ms. Gu, congratulations.
This is a huge scoop.

510
00:29:16,811 --> 00:29:18,659
Yes, thank you.

511
00:29:18,659 --> 00:29:20,192
[Investigative Reporting Team]

512
00:29:20,192 --> 00:29:22,203
Ms. Gu!

513
00:29:22,203 --> 00:29:24,947
Is it really okay for a rookie
to land an exclusive this quickly?

514
00:29:24,947 --> 00:29:26,355
You're going to make the seniors look bad.

515
00:29:26,355 --> 00:29:27,823
You owe us a treat. You have to treat us.

516
00:29:27,823 --> 00:29:31,347
- Actually, it's not my exclusive...
- What do you mean?

517
00:29:31,347 --> 00:29:34,475
How did we have such a talented person
at our company without knowing?

518
00:29:34,475 --> 00:29:36,419
How on earth did you scoop this?

519
00:29:36,419 --> 00:29:40,959
Actually, I wasn't the one who got it...

520
00:29:42,043 --> 00:29:43,351
She says she'll treat us, Chief.

521
00:29:43,351 --> 00:29:45,435
Come on, don't squeeze a rookie dry.

522
00:29:45,435 --> 00:29:48,459
Still, she should treat us all.
It's her first exclusive.

523
00:29:48,459 --> 00:29:52,359
[Chairman Cheon, Kingfisher Target,
Accused of Sexual Assault, Murder-for-Hire]

524
00:29:52,359 --> 00:29:53,726
[Investigative Reporting Team Reporter,
Gu Hae Na]

525
00:29:53,726 --> 00:29:56,659
[Related Articles]

526
00:30:10,447 --> 00:30:14,459
She wants to move up the final meeting.

527
00:30:15,099 --> 00:30:16,751
If possible, right away today.

528
00:30:16,751 --> 00:30:17,859
Today, right away?

529
00:30:17,859 --> 00:30:19,115
"Feint east, strike west."

530
00:30:19,115 --> 00:30:21,519
"Make noise in the east
and strike in the west."

531
00:30:21,519 --> 00:30:23,226
Where is Tae Min?

532
00:30:38,491 --> 00:30:40,231
When was the last time you washed your hair?

533
00:30:40,231 --> 00:30:43,315
Do you even wash your clothes?
Do you ever change your socks?

534
00:30:43,315 --> 00:30:45,926
At least wear shoes!

535
00:30:48,459 --> 00:30:50,859
Have you no consideration for your partner?

536
00:30:50,859 --> 00:30:54,567
Your hair's greasy, your clothes
are filthy, and your shoes stink.

537
00:30:54,567 --> 00:30:58,292
At this rate, I'll suffocate
before the meeting even starts!

538
00:31:04,775 --> 00:31:07,492
What... What are you doing?

539
00:31:12,679 --> 00:31:14,692
It was here.

540
00:31:15,707 --> 00:31:17,759
Darn it.

541
00:31:20,867 --> 00:31:24,787
This isn't the kind of scene I dreamed of.

542
00:31:24,787 --> 00:31:28,459
My dream was to someday
stand side by side with Kingfisher...

543
00:31:57,627 --> 00:31:59,783
He ordered a lot.

544
00:31:59,783 --> 00:32:01,492
Looks good.

545
00:32:14,311 --> 00:32:17,859
Oh, I'm starving. I'm starving.

546
00:32:19,843 --> 00:32:22,592
Alright, let's see.

547
00:32:23,271 --> 00:32:26,479
Sweet and sour pork,
pepper and veggie stir-fry,

548
00:32:26,479 --> 00:32:29,892
jjajangmyeon, jjajangmyeon...

549
00:32:32,727 --> 00:32:36,315
The punk who burned his own parents alive
sure has an appetite.

550
00:32:36,315 --> 00:32:38,092
Unbelievable.

551
00:32:38,092 --> 00:32:39,797
Does it make sense that he only got six years

552
00:32:39,797 --> 00:32:41,331
for burning his parents alive
for their inheritance?

553
00:32:41,331 --> 00:32:44,279
Claim diminished mental capacity
and write fifty apology letters a day.

554
00:32:44,279 --> 00:32:45,807
Who doesn't know that?

555
00:32:45,807 --> 00:32:48,283
That punk's all lies...

556
00:32:48,283 --> 00:32:49,983
Huh?

557
00:32:50,759 --> 00:32:52,926
- Ah, that darn fly.
- <i>Over to Kim Gyeong Ho.</i>

558
00:32:52,926 --> 00:32:54,619
<i>He gets it. Shoot!</i>

559
00:32:54,619 --> 00:32:56,319
<i>This is...</i>

560
00:33:05,215 --> 00:33:06,526
<i>Opposite side!</i>

561
00:33:06,526 --> 00:33:08,592
<i>Layup!</i>

562
00:33:08,592 --> 00:33:10,595
Darn it.

563
00:33:10,595 --> 00:33:12,099
Hey!

564
00:33:12,099 --> 00:33:13,192
Darn it, what?

565
00:33:13,192 --> 00:33:14,367
What?

566
00:33:14,367 --> 00:33:16,283
- <i>Now, he's running.</i>
- What happened?

567
00:33:16,283 --> 00:33:18,107
That's right, that's right!

568
00:33:18,107 --> 00:33:21,622
Oh, darn it!

569
00:33:27,067 --> 00:33:29,323
It's 10 milliliters of concentrated Mist S.

570
00:33:29,323 --> 00:33:31,915
Its casing is water-soluble,
so it dissolves on contact with water

571
00:33:31,915 --> 00:33:33,435
<i>and causes death within five minutes.</i>

572
00:33:33,435 --> 00:33:36,915
It breaks down within an hour,
so it won't show up even in an autopsy.

573
00:33:36,915 --> 00:33:38,563
<i>Ten seconds remaining.</i>

574
00:33:38,563 --> 00:33:42,415
Oh, there's not much time left. Hurry up!

575
00:33:42,415 --> 00:33:43,439
<i>Now, the remaining time.</i>

576
00:33:43,439 --> 00:33:46,047
<i>5 seconds, 4 seconds,</i>

577
00:33:46,047 --> 00:33:50,078
<i>3 seconds, 2 seconds, 1 second.</i>

578
00:33:50,078 --> 00:33:51,635
<i>He shoots!</i>

579
00:33:51,635 --> 00:33:53,292
<i>Beyond the 3-point line!</i>

580
00:33:53,292 --> 00:33:56,067
<i>Is it in? Is it going in?</i>

581
00:33:56,067 --> 00:33:57,687
<i>It's in!</i>

582
00:33:57,687 --> 00:34:00,692
- Yes!
- <i>Three-point buzzer-beater! Good!</i>

583
00:34:04,271 --> 00:34:06,292
<i>That wins the game!</i>

584
00:34:06,292 --> 00:34:09,999
- Hey, you had it in you.
- <i>What a way to finish the game.</i>

585
00:34:09,999 --> 00:34:11,631
Hey, you should've played like that
from the start.

586
00:34:11,631 --> 00:34:14,292
<i>Looks like they're ready for the playoffs.</i>

587
00:34:28,391 --> 00:34:30,091
Meeting clear.

588
00:34:30,091 --> 00:34:31,859
Nice!

589
00:35:01,735 --> 00:35:03,759
Rest in peace.

590
00:35:05,107 --> 00:35:08,992
If you see your parents,
make sure you apologize to them.

591
00:35:10,791 --> 00:35:12,759
That punk.

592
00:35:19,299 --> 00:35:22,507
We wrapped up our final meeting,

593
00:35:22,507 --> 00:35:24,643
so let's have a team dinner for once.

594
00:35:24,643 --> 00:35:27,327
How about beef? Let's have beef.

595
00:35:27,327 --> 00:35:30,979
This month's operating expenses
have been settled too.

596
00:35:30,979 --> 00:35:32,631
Oh, really?

597
00:35:32,631 --> 00:35:35,219
All right, then how about beef? Huh?

598
00:35:35,219 --> 00:35:36,783
Let's have beef, okay?

599
00:35:36,783 --> 00:35:39,826
How about beef? Let's have beef!

600
00:35:43,183 --> 00:35:45,859
<i>Yul going missing isn't your fault.</i>

601
00:35:46,475 --> 00:35:49,726
<i>So please don't cry. I'll find her for you.</i>

602
00:36:08,126 --> 00:36:11,399
<i>If you keep thinking about someone all day</i>

603
00:36:11,399 --> 00:36:14,067
<i>and smile every time they cross your mind,</i>

604
00:36:14,067 --> 00:36:17,035
<i>is that love?</i>

605
00:36:17,035 --> 00:36:18,735
[Mr. Tiger]
<i>Busy.</i>

606
00:36:19,459 --> 00:36:22,692
<i>I think I'm falling in love.</i>

607
00:36:24,492 --> 00:36:27,359
[Mr. Tiger]
<i>Hehe...</i>

608
00:36:27,359 --> 00:36:29,092
Jeez...

609
00:36:31,331 --> 00:36:34,559
<i>Forget it. What would you know about love?</i>

610
00:36:34,559 --> 00:36:35,826
<i>You're a lifelong single. What do you know?</i>

611
00:36:35,826 --> 00:36:37,559
And what about you?

612
00:36:41,195 --> 00:36:42,831
<i>Then tell me what to do.</i>

613
00:36:42,831 --> 00:36:45,659
<i>I've never felt this way before.
I don't know what to do.</i>

614
00:36:47,939 --> 00:36:49,607
<i>Just ask him to meet.</i>

615
00:36:49,607 --> 00:36:52,826
<i>You have to meet him before you can
even get rejected. Hehe...</i>

616
00:36:54,131 --> 00:36:56,279
<i>Is that really okay?</i>

617
00:36:56,279 --> 00:36:58,926
<i>Or just find a natural excuse to see him.</i>

618
00:37:00,827 --> 00:37:02,527
<i>How?</i>

619
00:37:03,535 --> 00:37:05,235
<i>Busy.</i>

620
00:37:06,707 --> 00:37:08,859
He doesn't know either.

621
00:37:11,226 --> 00:37:14,659
A natural excuse to meet?

622
00:37:23,335 --> 00:37:25,559
Oh, seriously...

623
00:37:33,115 --> 00:37:34,683
Se Ah, what brings you here at this hour?

624
00:37:34,683 --> 00:37:36,267
I came to see Yul!

625
00:37:36,267 --> 00:37:37,311
Auntie!

626
00:37:37,311 --> 00:37:40,407
- Looks so delicious.
- Sangju dried persimmons, Yul's favorite.

627
00:37:40,407 --> 00:37:44,011
Open wide! Here we go! Whoosh!

628
00:37:44,011 --> 00:37:46,539
- Wider! Say, "Ah!"
- "Ah!"

629
00:37:46,539 --> 00:37:49,107
Commander, that's not
the right route. Rerouting.

630
00:37:49,107 --> 00:37:52,187
No, not this way. I don't want to eat it.

631
00:37:52,187 --> 00:37:54,039
- Oh, my.
- Daddy!

632
00:37:54,039 --> 00:37:55,783
Yum, it's good!

633
00:37:55,783 --> 00:37:57,483
Yul, say "Ah!"

634
00:37:59,723 --> 00:38:01,399
- Yum, it's good!
- It's good, right?

635
00:38:01,399 --> 00:38:03,687
Eat up.

636
00:38:03,687 --> 00:38:06,995
Bo Na, work must be really
tough for you lately, right?

637
00:38:06,995 --> 00:38:09,826
Not really. He's been helping me a lot,
so I'm doing fine.

638
00:38:09,826 --> 00:38:11,147
And I have a reliable sister-in-law too.

639
00:38:11,147 --> 00:38:14,059
Oh, I haven't done anything.

640
00:38:14,927 --> 00:38:16,279
Se Ah, did you come
because you need pocket money?

641
00:38:16,279 --> 00:38:17,971
No.

642
00:38:17,971 --> 00:38:21,187
How are things with your coworkers?
Are they treating you well?

643
00:38:21,187 --> 00:38:24,851
They've been really helpful,
so I've adjusted without much trouble.

644
00:38:24,851 --> 00:38:28,695
Oh, they must all be wonderful people.

645
00:38:28,695 --> 00:38:32,795
Tae Seong, shouldn't you treat them
to a meal sometime?

646
00:38:32,795 --> 00:38:34,455
- All of a sudden?
- Bo Na,

647
00:38:34,455 --> 00:38:37,926
since you got married,
have you ever had a housewarming party?

648
00:38:38,939 --> 00:38:40,439
A housewarming party?

649
00:38:40,439 --> 00:38:43,392
Inviting those people over,
showing them the house,

650
00:38:43,392 --> 00:38:45,179
and serving them food, that kind of thing.

651
00:38:45,179 --> 00:38:47,926
No, I've never really thought about it.

652
00:38:51,358 --> 00:38:52,823
Tae Seong, don't you know that nowadays,

653
00:38:52,823 --> 00:38:55,011
a husband's support
is just as important as a wife's?

654
00:38:55,011 --> 00:38:57,771
Working moms already
have enough pressure at work.

655
00:38:57,771 --> 00:39:02,092
You need to take care of things
so work is easier for her, right?

656
00:39:04,367 --> 00:39:06,335
You've got a point.

657
00:39:06,335 --> 00:39:08,630
Bo Na, they've been so supportive of you

658
00:39:08,630 --> 00:39:11,351
since you returned to work after three years,

659
00:39:11,351 --> 00:39:14,919
so why not show your appreciation
by treating them to a nice home-cooked meal?

660
00:39:14,919 --> 00:39:18,143
That's what makes life feel warm and fun.

661
00:39:18,143 --> 00:39:21,618
Think of it as a company dinner! Huh?

662
00:39:21,618 --> 00:39:23,359
A company dinner?

663
00:39:27,592 --> 00:39:34,059
Why would Director Yoo summon us
to her home herself?

664
00:39:34,751 --> 00:39:37,526
She's never really had people over before.

665
00:39:38,839 --> 00:39:42,051
Maybe it's some kind of cover
to avoid drawing attention?

666
00:39:42,051 --> 00:39:45,267
Our Director Yoo isn't exactly the type
to put on an act like that, okay?

667
00:39:45,267 --> 00:39:47,499
What should we bring as a gift?

668
00:39:47,499 --> 00:39:50,175
Nothing beats toilet paper.
May everything go smoothly.

669
00:39:50,175 --> 00:39:53,579
Come on, diffusers are the trend these days.

670
00:39:53,579 --> 00:39:55,383
How about a wine glass set?

671
00:39:55,383 --> 00:39:58,059
Booze is better than glasses.

672
00:39:59,767 --> 00:40:02,943
But is Manager Tae Min not coming with us?

673
00:40:02,943 --> 00:40:05,099
Manager Tae doesn't really go out
unless it's for a meeting.

674
00:40:05,099 --> 00:40:07,147
He's a total homebody.

675
00:40:07,147 --> 00:40:10,926
Yeah, he'd probably just be a burden.
Especially since she's got kids at home.

676
00:40:11,591 --> 00:40:14,175
How about a nice mood lamp?

677
00:40:14,175 --> 00:40:15,875
A mood lamp?

678
00:40:17,283 --> 00:40:19,543
Let's keep it simple.

679
00:40:19,543 --> 00:40:21,792
You know what I mean, right?

680
00:40:22,539 --> 00:40:24,692
My favorite wine.

681
00:40:26,955 --> 00:40:29,259
- Okay.
- So you'd already made up your mind.

682
00:40:29,931 --> 00:40:32,392
- Pork belly and ribs are on sale today.
- Oh, ribs!

683
00:40:32,392 --> 00:40:33,884
- Have a look.
- Okay.

684
00:40:33,884 --> 00:40:36,383
- How about this?
- Pork belly and short ribs are on sale.

685
00:40:36,383 --> 00:40:38,247
It's huge, right?

686
00:40:38,247 --> 00:40:39,612
Alright.

687
00:40:39,612 --> 00:40:41,424
There we go.

688
00:40:44,423 --> 00:40:47,326
What is next?

689
00:40:47,931 --> 00:40:51,859
Frozen pollock and two mackerel, right?

690
00:40:52,871 --> 00:40:55,292
- Let's go.
- Mommy, squid!

691
00:40:55,292 --> 00:40:57,492
Should we get squid now?

692
00:40:57,492 --> 00:40:58,875
Veggies, veggies!

693
00:40:58,875 --> 00:41:00,371
Huh? Should we get veggies now?

694
00:41:00,371 --> 00:41:02,692
Okay, we can get veggies now.

695
00:41:03,687 --> 00:41:04,759
What was next after that?

696
00:41:04,759 --> 00:41:07,057
Wow, look at that cart.

697
00:41:07,057 --> 00:41:10,126
She is really excited.

698
00:41:11,715 --> 00:41:13,655
We should've done this sooner.

699
00:41:13,655 --> 00:41:15,919
But when I think about it,
she's really something.

700
00:41:15,919 --> 00:41:19,327
There's so much she's never done,
and so much she's never experienced.

701
00:41:19,327 --> 00:41:22,258
How on earth has she lived her life?

702
00:41:22,258 --> 00:41:23,299
Do you know anything about it?

703
00:41:23,299 --> 00:41:24,999
Huh?

704
00:41:26,559 --> 00:41:29,592
I'm her husband. How would I not know?

705
00:41:30,467 --> 00:41:32,644
You clearly don't!

706
00:41:32,644 --> 00:41:34,463
Bo Na!

707
00:41:34,463 --> 00:41:36,726
Tae Seong, go grab a cart. A cart.

708
00:41:36,726 --> 00:41:38,592
- Okay.
- Bo Na!

709
00:41:38,592 --> 00:41:39,592
Yeah, Se Ah.

710
00:41:39,592 --> 00:41:40,627
Hold onto this for a second.

711
00:41:40,627 --> 00:41:41,827
Huh?

712
00:41:41,827 --> 00:41:43,771
Oh, well... Bo Na.

713
00:41:43,771 --> 00:41:46,659
The hacker who came
to the playground that time...

714
00:41:47,794 --> 00:41:49,259
I mean, your colleague.

715
00:41:49,259 --> 00:41:51,355
Assistant Manager Ki Yeong Do?

716
00:41:51,355 --> 00:41:54,643
So his name is Ki Yeong Do.

717
00:41:54,643 --> 00:41:56,583
What a good name...

718
00:41:56,583 --> 00:41:59,126
Oh, don't worry.

719
00:42:00,179 --> 00:42:01,879
Thank you.

720
00:42:03,195 --> 00:42:08,259
Do you know what kind of food he likes?

721
00:42:09,261 --> 00:42:10,961
I'm not sure.

722
00:42:11,652 --> 00:42:12,923
Oh, well...

723
00:42:12,923 --> 00:42:18,327
Since he helped us so much
in finding Yul, so... to repay him!

724
00:42:18,327 --> 00:42:22,911
Wouldn't it be nice to include
at least one side dish he likes

725
00:42:22,911 --> 00:42:25,895
as a small token of gratitude?

726
00:42:25,895 --> 00:42:27,826
Now that you mention it, you're right.

727
00:42:27,826 --> 00:42:29,526
What should we make?

728
00:42:30,347 --> 00:42:31,819
He's a picky eater, though.

729
00:42:31,819 --> 00:42:35,035
Oh, he's a light eater.

730
00:42:35,035 --> 00:42:40,191
Still, his hand keeps going back to it,
that kind of thing?

731
00:42:49,415 --> 00:42:50,611
Oh! Hello!

732
00:42:50,611 --> 00:42:53,207
- Hello, nice to meet you.
- Nice to meet you.

733
00:42:53,207 --> 00:42:55,367
- Shall we go in?
- Yeah, please come in.

734
00:42:55,367 --> 00:42:57,292
- Let's see.
- Excuse us.

735
00:42:58,267 --> 00:42:59,267
What a nice place, right?

736
00:42:59,267 --> 00:43:00,967
Yeah.

737
00:43:01,663 --> 00:43:02,959
- Come on in.
- Okay.

738
00:43:02,959 --> 00:43:04,783
Please come in. Honey!

739
00:43:04,783 --> 00:43:05,783
- Yeah.
- They're here.

740
00:43:05,783 --> 00:43:08,039
You're here?

741
00:43:08,039 --> 00:43:10,759
Thanks for coming all this way.

742
00:43:12,083 --> 00:43:14,415
This is my husband, Kwon Tae Seong.

743
00:43:14,415 --> 00:43:15,919
Nice to meet you.

744
00:43:15,919 --> 00:43:19,087
I should've invited you over sooner.
I feel like it's so late.

745
00:43:19,087 --> 00:43:20,751
Thank you so much for coming.

746
00:43:20,751 --> 00:43:24,104
We're the ones who should be thanking you
for inviting us into your home.

747
00:43:24,104 --> 00:43:25,283
Oh, not at all.

748
00:43:25,283 --> 00:43:29,359
Oh, my, your husband is so handsome.

749
00:43:31,355 --> 00:43:32,659
Really?

750
00:43:32,659 --> 00:43:34,319
Yul, say hello.

751
00:43:34,319 --> 00:43:35,803
They're Mommy's friends from work.

752
00:43:35,803 --> 00:43:37,047
Hello.

753
00:43:37,047 --> 00:43:39,926
- Hello.
- So you're Yul?

754
00:43:39,926 --> 00:43:42,035
Mind if we look around?

755
00:43:42,035 --> 00:43:43,763
- Of course, go ahead.
- Sure, make yourselves at home.

756
00:43:43,763 --> 00:43:45,095
Yes, make yourselves at home. Please come in.

757
00:43:45,095 --> 00:43:46,695
Why did you bring so much?

758
00:43:46,695 --> 00:43:48,375
- It's all for you, Director Yoo.
- You can definitely tell

759
00:43:48,375 --> 00:43:50,694
a child lives here.

760
00:43:50,694 --> 00:43:52,426
It's so cozy and cute.

761
00:43:53,235 --> 00:43:54,911
Half the stuff is for the baby.

762
00:43:54,911 --> 00:43:57,099
Finally, I get to see it.

763
00:43:57,099 --> 00:44:00,667
I was really curious
what it looked like inside.

764
00:44:00,667 --> 00:44:04,059
Mommy! Auntie Se Ah became a princess!

765
00:44:07,923 --> 00:44:09,623
Oh, really?

766
00:44:13,135 --> 00:44:15,571
This is my youngest sister.

767
00:44:15,571 --> 00:44:19,059
She came by to help out today.

768
00:44:19,691 --> 00:44:22,503
Your sister even helped
with the housewarming party?

769
00:44:22,503 --> 00:44:24,659
That's so sweet of her.

770
00:44:25,559 --> 00:44:27,526
Nice to meet you.

771
00:44:27,526 --> 00:44:29,926
I'm Kwon Se Ah.

772
00:44:33,699 --> 00:44:35,399
Honey.

773
00:44:36,931 --> 00:44:38,631
Have you been drinking?

774
00:44:42,127 --> 00:44:44,867
- Wow!
- Oh, my, the table's going to collapse.

775
00:44:44,867 --> 00:44:47,639
You didn't make all this yourself, did you?

776
00:44:47,639 --> 00:44:51,017
Wait, you're saying you made
this entire feast yourself?

777
00:44:51,017 --> 00:44:53,646
- Well...
- I was going to order some of it,

778
00:44:53,646 --> 00:44:55,935
but she insisted on
making everything herself.

779
00:44:55,935 --> 00:44:58,367
I made it all.

780
00:44:58,367 --> 00:45:01,707
They say a housewarming meal
should be made with care,

781
00:45:01,707 --> 00:45:04,675
so I put my heart into it.

782
00:45:04,675 --> 00:45:08,359
This is a classic festive dish made with
glass noodles, meat, and vegetables,

783
00:45:08,359 --> 00:45:11,295
all beautifully combined.

784
00:45:11,295 --> 00:45:15,267
It's a hearty meat dish
that's perfect for serving guests.

785
00:45:15,267 --> 00:45:19,951
And these pancakes, easy to eat,
but you can feel the effort put into them.

786
00:45:19,951 --> 00:45:22,135
I made it all myself.

787
00:45:22,135 --> 00:45:25,091
Well, since I came back,

788
00:45:25,091 --> 00:45:29,226
you've all helped me so much to readjust.
I'm really grateful.

789
00:45:31,083 --> 00:45:35,526
I really wanted to make you all
a warm, home-cooked meal.

790
00:45:36,447 --> 00:45:40,563
I've been wanting to say this for a while.

791
00:45:40,563 --> 00:45:42,359
There's not much, but please eat your fill.

792
00:45:42,359 --> 00:45:44,891
Oh, come on.

793
00:45:44,891 --> 00:45:47,259
Look at all this food.

794
00:45:47,259 --> 00:45:49,051
I think we're really going to feast today.

795
00:45:49,051 --> 00:45:50,363
Eat plenty.

796
00:45:50,363 --> 00:45:51,859
Thank you for the meal!

797
00:45:51,859 --> 00:45:53,992
- Thank you for the meal!
- Thank you.

798
00:45:53,992 --> 00:45:55,726
Come on, dig in.

799
00:45:56,379 --> 00:45:58,626
- Enjoy your meal.
- Yeah, thanks.

800
00:46:03,547 --> 00:46:07,139
I heard from my sister-in-law
that you sometimes enjoy this,

801
00:46:07,139 --> 00:46:12,026
so I made some.

802
00:46:12,659 --> 00:46:14,559
I hope you enjoy it.

803
00:46:15,879 --> 00:46:17,823
Eat up, Se Ah.

804
00:46:17,823 --> 00:46:19,475
Want some short ribs?

805
00:46:19,475 --> 00:46:20,579
- Yeah!
- I'll cut it for you.

806
00:46:20,579 --> 00:46:21,602
- It's good.
- Honey, I'll do it.

807
00:46:21,602 --> 00:46:23,879
- You didn't even have lunch.
- Honey, eat a lot.

808
00:46:23,879 --> 00:46:26,115
Honey, want some of that?

809
00:46:26,115 --> 00:46:29,091
You two are so sweet.

810
00:46:29,091 --> 00:46:32,926
Can I ask how you two first met?

811
00:46:34,239 --> 00:46:36,995
We just...

812
00:46:36,995 --> 00:46:39,853
met like that, coming and going.

813
00:46:39,853 --> 00:46:42,727
Actually, a pickpocket brought us together.

814
00:46:42,727 --> 00:46:44,126
- A pickpocket?
- Yeah.

815
00:46:44,126 --> 00:46:46,675
About eight years ago,
I was covering a pickpocketing case

816
00:46:46,675 --> 00:46:48,235
and suffered a serious head injury.

817
00:46:48,235 --> 00:46:52,207
Oh, goodness. So you went through
quite a terrible ordeal.

818
00:46:52,207 --> 00:46:58,599
But luckily, a woman called an ambulance,
and I barely survived.

819
00:46:58,599 --> 00:47:00,611
The doctors said things could've
turned out much worse

820
00:47:00,611 --> 00:47:02,992
if she'd called even a little later.

821
00:47:03,711 --> 00:47:07,167
After about four months, when I finally
woke up and was able to walk again,

822
00:47:07,167 --> 00:47:11,923
I went up to the hospital rooftop,
and that's where I met Bo Na.

823
00:47:11,923 --> 00:47:16,295
- <i>That day, I fell for Bo Na's bright smile</i>
- Come down!

824
00:47:16,295 --> 00:47:18,855
- at first sight.
- Yes.

825
00:47:18,855 --> 00:47:21,326
How romantic!

826
00:47:21,326 --> 00:47:25,859
I didn't know you two had such a love story.

827
00:47:25,859 --> 00:47:29,191
That's so touching. A love that began
on the boundary between life and death.

828
00:47:29,191 --> 00:47:31,187
Oh, right.

829
00:47:31,187 --> 00:47:36,949
Do you happen to know who the woman was
who called an ambulance back then?

830
00:47:36,949 --> 00:47:40,799
Actually, as soon as I woke up,
I checked with the emergency call center,

831
00:47:40,799 --> 00:47:44,127
but the call was made from my phone,
so I couldn't get her contact info.

832
00:47:44,127 --> 00:47:46,375
And they couldn't remember
anything about the caller

833
00:47:46,375 --> 00:47:48,563
other than that she was a woman.

834
00:47:48,563 --> 00:47:52,392
But she'll probably be greatly blessed.

835
00:47:52,392 --> 00:47:55,347
She saved your life. Don't you think?

836
00:47:55,347 --> 00:47:58,327
Then wasn't it that woman,
rather than the pickpocket,

837
00:47:58,327 --> 00:48:01,026
who brought you two together?

838
00:48:02,631 --> 00:48:04,502
Now that she mentions it, that's true.

839
00:48:04,502 --> 00:48:08,259
I should find her somehow
and thank her, right?

840
00:48:08,259 --> 00:48:09,903
- You should.
- Yes, I'll do it.

841
00:48:09,903 --> 00:48:12,559
It's getting cold. Please eat up.

842
00:48:13,771 --> 00:48:16,526
Well... Assistant Manager Ki.

843
00:48:17,139 --> 00:48:19,563
You should try some meat too.

844
00:48:19,563 --> 00:48:21,911
Here... Oh, my.

845
00:48:21,911 --> 00:48:22,911
Oh, no!

846
00:48:22,911 --> 00:48:25,555
Hold on, let me...

847
00:48:25,555 --> 00:48:27,571
Oh, what do I do? Wet wipes.

848
00:48:27,571 --> 00:48:29,567
I'm so sorry, Assistant Manager Ki.

849
00:48:29,567 --> 00:48:31,115
It's okay.

850
00:48:31,115 --> 00:48:32,667
Do you have any cold beer?

851
00:48:32,667 --> 00:48:33,667
Beer?

852
00:48:33,667 --> 00:48:36,559
Sure, I'll get you one right away.

853
00:48:37,595 --> 00:48:39,627
Here.

854
00:48:39,627 --> 00:48:41,759
Let me open it for you.

855
00:49:01,787 --> 00:49:03,487
At least have this...

856
00:49:14,026 --> 00:49:15,699
[Eight Years Ago, Spring]

857
00:49:15,699 --> 00:49:18,747
[Personnel Profile]
I never applied for a job at this company.

858
00:49:18,747 --> 00:49:19,983
There must be some mistake...

859
00:49:19,983 --> 00:49:25,047
You must've been surprised to suddenly
receive a job application by email.

860
00:49:25,047 --> 00:49:27,659
You were kidnapped as a child.

861
00:49:27,659 --> 00:49:31,592
You majored in psychology,
and your specialty is hacking, huh?

862
00:49:34,135 --> 00:49:36,626
Durumi Electronics, Sales Team 3.

863
00:49:37,419 --> 00:49:40,392
It seems like they do different work
from other departments.

864
00:49:47,647 --> 00:49:48,695
Go on.

865
00:49:48,695 --> 00:49:52,783
The sales records look subtly
different from those of other departments.

866
00:49:52,783 --> 00:49:56,159
It felt like they'd taken real data
and pieced it together, you know?

867
00:49:56,159 --> 00:49:58,619
The fieldwork ratio
in the work logs is unusual too.

868
00:49:58,619 --> 00:50:03,011
So did you figure out what they actually do?

869
00:50:03,011 --> 00:50:07,092
Only that it's illegal?

870
00:50:08,139 --> 00:50:10,087
That's right.

871
00:50:10,087 --> 00:50:14,726
Sales Team 3 selects
and eliminates criminals.

872
00:50:16,635 --> 00:50:20,551
For several reasons,
I like your qualifications, Mr. Ki Yeong Do.

873
00:50:20,551 --> 00:50:23,292
What happens if I turn you down?

874
00:50:25,883 --> 00:50:29,359
We only make offers to people
who won't refuse.

875
00:50:30,199 --> 00:50:34,126
And if I still refuse, will I be killed?

876
00:50:39,783 --> 00:50:42,059
Then you'll have to keep our secret.

877
00:50:50,575 --> 00:50:54,026
What are you going to do?
Will you keep the secret?

878
00:50:58,999 --> 00:51:00,792
You scared?

879
00:51:15,431 --> 00:51:17,726
Eat up and relax, rookie.

880
00:51:25,955 --> 00:51:29,226
This is the best cure for stress. Eat.

881
00:51:53,075 --> 00:51:57,526
I'm done. I'm done.

882
00:51:58,199 --> 00:52:01,179
Ugh, just get out of here.

883
00:52:01,179 --> 00:52:03,192
Just go out and die.

884
00:52:07,892 --> 00:52:09,671
Look at this.

885
00:52:09,671 --> 00:52:11,626
Wow!

886
00:52:11,626 --> 00:52:13,127
- Oh, dear.
- Yul.

887
00:52:13,127 --> 00:52:15,379
Want some strawberries?

888
00:52:15,379 --> 00:52:17,419
- Let's all raise our glasses.
- Cheers!

889
00:52:17,419 --> 00:52:20,699
I'm sorry for causing a scene.

890
00:52:20,699 --> 00:52:22,819
I'm going to head home first.

891
00:52:22,819 --> 00:52:23,819
- Where are you going?
- Perfect.

892
00:52:23,819 --> 00:52:27,163
Assistant Manager Ki is heading home,
so you can walk him to the main road.

893
00:52:27,163 --> 00:52:29,095
He's taking the subway, so take him out
through the back entrance.

894
00:52:29,095 --> 00:52:31,159
- Me?
- Yeah.

895
00:52:31,159 --> 00:52:32,159
- Why?
- What do you mean, why?

896
00:52:32,159 --> 00:52:34,499
He doesn't know the way.

897
00:52:34,499 --> 00:52:37,359
Oh, yeah. Go ahead.

898
00:52:37,359 --> 00:52:39,027
We'll stay a little longer.

899
00:52:39,027 --> 00:52:41,189
- Alright.
- Please eat.

900
00:52:41,189 --> 00:52:43,026
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

901
00:52:44,251 --> 00:52:46,131
Well, Assistant Manager Ki!

902
00:52:46,131 --> 00:52:49,847
I'll make sure to wash your clothes
and return them.

903
00:52:49,847 --> 00:52:51,547
Please do.

904
00:52:52,663 --> 00:52:55,203
Are you very upset?

905
00:52:55,203 --> 00:52:56,903
I'm not happy.

906
00:52:57,891 --> 00:52:59,307
I guess you're pretty upset.

907
00:52:59,307 --> 00:53:01,626
It's because of me...

908
00:53:13,655 --> 00:53:15,859
Does your brother not have hands?

909
00:53:16,707 --> 00:53:18,407
Hands?

910
00:53:22,891 --> 00:53:24,591
Hands?

911
00:53:31,759 --> 00:53:34,092
When will you return my clothes?

912
00:53:35,491 --> 00:53:37,592
Soon? Yeah...

913
00:53:39,515 --> 00:53:43,559
The day you return my clothes,
let's go on a date.

914
00:53:59,439 --> 00:54:02,892
A... date?

915
00:54:06,915 --> 00:54:09,659
That was delicious. I'm stuffed.

916
00:54:10,675 --> 00:54:13,775
By the way, we did okay, right?

917
00:54:13,775 --> 00:54:16,026
Yeah, I think we did.

918
00:54:17,659 --> 00:54:19,759
We didn't make any mistakes, right?

919
00:54:20,471 --> 00:54:22,403
I don't think so.

920
00:54:22,403 --> 00:54:24,103
Good.

921
00:54:25,435 --> 00:54:30,259
Honestly, Director Yoo's cooking
isn't that great, right?

922
00:54:34,999 --> 00:54:38,475
Do we really not need to
erase the CCTV footage?

923
00:54:38,475 --> 00:54:40,359
Oh, Team Leader.

924
00:54:40,359 --> 00:54:42,163
We're not here for a meeting today.

925
00:54:42,163 --> 00:54:43,355
Right, right.

926
00:54:43,355 --> 00:54:46,192
Hey, let's keep it normal. Just act normal.

927
00:54:52,231 --> 00:54:53,939
Oh, go on in.

928
00:54:53,939 --> 00:54:55,219
Yeah, yeah.

929
00:54:55,219 --> 00:54:57,192
Thank you.

930
00:55:01,855 --> 00:55:03,555
Excuse me!

931
00:55:04,811 --> 00:55:07,092
I think you dropped something.

932
00:55:09,771 --> 00:55:11,471
Thank you.

933
00:55:12,475 --> 00:55:14,175
Thank you.

934
00:55:23,055 --> 00:55:24,992
Let's all go.

935
00:55:30,027 --> 00:55:31,159
Mr. Lee!

936
00:55:31,159 --> 00:55:32,671
Oh, my princess!

937
00:55:32,671 --> 00:55:35,751
Wow, my princess!

938
00:55:35,751 --> 00:55:39,411
Mr. Lee, have you caught a lot of bad guys?

939
00:55:39,411 --> 00:55:41,147
I caught this many.

940
00:55:41,147 --> 00:55:43,711
Oh, Yul.

941
00:55:43,711 --> 00:55:45,539
Now, stand at attention!

942
00:55:45,539 --> 00:55:48,939
I protect good kids like you, Yul. I'm...

943
00:55:48,939 --> 00:55:50,055
A police officer!

944
00:55:50,055 --> 00:55:52,479
That's right! Good job.

945
00:55:52,479 --> 00:55:53,763
- Let's go.
- You came earlier than expected.

946
00:55:53,763 --> 00:55:54,951
Guess you're not too busy?

947
00:55:54,951 --> 00:55:58,339
Hey, Bo Na is making braised ribs.
What could be more important than that?

948
00:55:58,339 --> 00:56:01,659
- Go play.
- Dong Jin, you're here?

949
00:56:01,659 --> 00:56:03,623
Thanks for inviting me again.

950
00:56:03,623 --> 00:56:05,335
Oh, it's nothing.

951
00:56:05,335 --> 00:56:08,455
Why does she always call you
whenever she cooks something special?

952
00:56:08,455 --> 00:56:10,587
That's becoming a bad habit.

953
00:56:10,587 --> 00:56:15,123
I may be unlucky with friends,
but I sure lucked out with my friend's wife.

954
00:56:15,123 --> 00:56:17,492
Yeah, you should focus on
finding your wife instead.

955
00:56:18,347 --> 00:56:19,855
Please come by more often.

956
00:56:19,855 --> 00:56:22,955
Yul gets so excited
whenever I tell her you're coming.

957
00:56:22,955 --> 00:56:24,723
Got it. I will.

958
00:56:24,723 --> 00:56:27,591
Anyway, Bo Na, you must be tired
after returning to work.

959
00:56:27,591 --> 00:56:28,626
Does he help you a lot?

960
00:56:28,626 --> 00:56:31,743
He's been so sheltered.
I doubt he knows how to do much.

961
00:56:31,743 --> 00:56:34,275
I'm really good at everything now.

962
00:56:34,275 --> 00:56:36,855
Honey, what else should I do?
Just say the word.

963
00:56:36,855 --> 00:56:40,039
He always means well,
but he's not exactly talented...

964
00:56:40,039 --> 00:56:42,427
Just a moment. I'll go get something for you.

965
00:56:42,427 --> 00:56:45,315
Thank you. I'll repay the favor.

966
00:56:45,315 --> 00:56:47,626
- Sit down, sit down.
- No, it's fine.

967
00:56:48,715 --> 00:56:49,991
Did you have guests over?

968
00:56:49,991 --> 00:56:51,695
Yeah, my wife's coworkers.

969
00:56:51,695 --> 00:56:54,159
They must be the ones who just left.

970
00:56:54,159 --> 00:56:55,383
Did you see them?

971
00:56:55,383 --> 00:56:57,007
Yeah, in front of the elevator
on the first floor.

972
00:56:57,007 --> 00:56:59,526
They seemed really nice.

973
00:57:03,455 --> 00:57:05,239
Looks like I'll be eating
home-cooked meals all week.

974
00:57:05,239 --> 00:57:07,419
Oh, Ms. Bo Na has always...

975
00:57:07,419 --> 00:57:09,551
I helped out with that every time.

976
00:57:09,551 --> 00:57:10,919
You just should say "thank you."

977
00:57:10,919 --> 00:57:14,279
What part? Tell me so I can throw it out.

978
00:57:14,279 --> 00:57:17,692
You said you'd repay the favor. With what?

979
00:57:18,339 --> 00:57:20,091
Do I have money? Do I have connections?

980
00:57:20,091 --> 00:57:22,153
Wow, the ink's barely dry
on your verbal promise,

981
00:57:22,153 --> 00:57:23,331
and you're already like this.

982
00:57:23,331 --> 00:57:27,126
What else can I do but protect? I'm a cop.

983
00:57:28,595 --> 00:57:30,067
Except you, you punk.

984
00:57:30,067 --> 00:57:33,159
I'm only going to protect
your kind wife and pretty Yul.

985
00:57:33,803 --> 00:57:36,726
I'll take care of protecting
my wife and daughter myself.

986
00:57:40,271 --> 00:57:45,099
Make sure you take extra good care of them
on birthdays and holidays.

987
00:57:45,099 --> 00:57:47,226
Not having family

988
00:57:48,071 --> 00:57:51,226
can be terribly lonely and painful.

989
00:58:26,575 --> 00:58:29,795
So what were you curious about?

990
00:58:29,795 --> 00:58:32,447
So you didn't write
the Cheon Seong Gil article after all?

991
00:58:32,447 --> 00:58:34,826
We wrote it together, with a junior reporter.

992
00:58:36,095 --> 00:58:38,043
If you don't want to talk, then that's fine.

993
00:58:38,043 --> 00:58:42,026
Anyway, thanks to that article,
Kingfisher's reputation was saved.

994
00:58:45,087 --> 00:58:48,539
Are you still getting played
by Kingfisher these days?

995
00:58:48,539 --> 00:58:53,226
Man, he's really going all out
since he came back.

996
00:58:53,911 --> 00:58:57,095
He's never operated this tightly before.

997
00:58:57,095 --> 00:58:59,159
If he takes another hiatus,

998
00:58:59,159 --> 00:59:02,107
he'll be back sweeping up
criminals all over the world.

999
00:59:02,107 --> 00:59:04,063
It's the second time.

1000
00:59:04,063 --> 00:59:05,267
- What?
- The hiatus.

1001
00:59:05,267 --> 00:59:07,043
There was one eight years ago, remember?

1002
00:59:07,043 --> 00:59:09,192
After that World Cup incident.

1003
00:59:09,192 --> 00:59:11,219
Oh...

1004
00:59:11,219 --> 00:59:12,392
Was it nine months back then?

1005
00:59:12,392 --> 00:59:14,759
When he came back, everyone was curious too,

1006
00:59:14,759 --> 00:59:16,926
wondering what had happened during that time.

1007
00:59:16,926 --> 00:59:20,379
I know what happened to me during that time.

1008
00:59:20,379 --> 00:59:23,383
I met Yoo Bo Na.

1009
00:59:23,383 --> 00:59:26,975
Were you the one who saved
Mr. Kwon Tae Seong that day?

1010
00:59:26,975 --> 00:59:28,392
<i>Yeah.</i>

1011
00:59:28,392 --> 00:59:29,726
Why?

1012
00:59:29,726 --> 00:59:31,271
Because I wanted to.

1013
00:59:31,271 --> 00:59:33,703
It could have been dangerous.

1014
00:59:33,703 --> 00:59:37,023
It was. Luckily, it wasn't.

1015
00:59:37,023 --> 00:59:39,379
You were secretly glad back then.

1016
00:59:39,379 --> 00:59:42,459
After Kingfisher came back
from the first hiatus.

1017
00:59:42,459 --> 00:59:44,259
I thought you'd feel the same way this time.

1018
00:59:44,259 --> 00:59:49,995
You used to want so badly
to meet Kingfisher. Lost interest now?

1019
00:59:49,995 --> 00:59:51,659
We can't meet.

1020
00:59:51,659 --> 00:59:55,635
<i>What happened after that?</i>

1021
00:59:55,635 --> 00:59:59,311
He... saved me.

1022
00:59:59,311 --> 01:00:01,659
And I came back.

1023
01:00:01,659 --> 01:00:03,203
Then...

1024
01:00:03,203 --> 01:00:05,639
That's right. My husband.

1025
01:00:05,639 --> 01:00:08,259
He's the one who brought me back.

1026
01:00:08,259 --> 01:00:10,292
<i>He shouldn't have come back.</i>

1027
01:00:11,159 --> 01:00:12,339
Not this time...

1028
01:00:12,339 --> 01:00:15,807
And the one who brought me
back as Kingfisher this time...

1029
01:00:15,807 --> 01:00:17,795
He shouldn't have come.

1030
01:00:17,795 --> 01:00:19,719
<i>Kwon Tae Seong,</i>

1031
01:00:19,719 --> 01:00:21,419
it's him.

1032
01:00:25,855 --> 01:00:31,059
It's cold out. How about we
talk about it again when it warms up?

1033
01:00:31,983 --> 01:00:34,403
I've thought about it for a long time.

1034
01:00:34,403 --> 01:00:37,835
I know, but who knows?

1035
01:00:37,835 --> 01:00:41,059
Maybe when the flowers bloom
and spring comes, you'll change your mind.

1036
01:00:44,343 --> 01:00:47,226
I don't want to do anything anymore.

1037
01:00:51,339 --> 01:00:52,743
Take some time off starting today.

1038
01:00:52,743 --> 01:00:55,131
Rest as much as you need.

1039
01:00:55,131 --> 01:00:59,203
Right, this is the perfect time for a trip.

1040
01:00:59,203 --> 01:01:02,623
Anyone have a travel spot
to recommend for Yoo Bo Na?

1041
01:01:02,623 --> 01:01:06,892
Somewhere with mountains, fresh air,
and nothing you have to do.

1042
01:01:08,635 --> 01:01:10,335
That's...

1043
01:01:14,555 --> 01:01:16,087
What about here?

1044
01:01:16,087 --> 01:01:19,715
It's quiet, there's no one around,
and there's no cell service.

1045
01:01:19,715 --> 01:01:22,692
They even serve three meals
a day on schedule.

1046
01:01:24,859 --> 01:01:26,759
Right, a trip should be by the sea.

1047
01:01:26,759 --> 01:01:29,079
Somewhere wide open, right?

1048
01:01:29,079 --> 01:01:31,959
Yeah, you can take a boat. It's perfect.

1049
01:01:31,959 --> 01:01:33,999
- Go there.
- And if you come back

1050
01:01:33,999 --> 01:01:38,575
and still feel the same,
I'll accept your resignation.

1051
01:01:38,575 --> 01:01:40,275
Okay?

1052
01:02:06,103 --> 01:02:09,739
Oh, dear, she's not eating.
I don't know why she's like that.

1053
01:02:09,739 --> 01:02:11,623
Did she skip another meal?

1054
01:02:11,623 --> 01:02:14,792
I'm worried, so worried.

1055
01:04:46,779 --> 01:04:49,051
What do you think of
when you see icicles, Bo Na?

1056
01:04:49,051 --> 01:04:51,583
It'd be perfect for piercing
a vital spot in one go.

1057
01:04:51,583 --> 01:04:54,791
I've never really looked at something
and thought it was pretty.

1058
01:04:54,791 --> 01:04:56,267
I'll show you plenty of beautiful things
from now on.

1059
01:04:56,267 --> 01:04:59,127
They've closed all the roads
into the mountain since yesterday afternoon.

1060
01:04:59,127 --> 01:05:01,226
Looks like we're stranded.

1061
01:05:02,211 --> 01:05:03,927
Bo Na!

1062
01:05:03,927 --> 01:05:05,479
Why did you do that
right after being released?

1063
01:05:05,479 --> 01:05:07,635
Isn't all of this because the police
can't catch Kingfisher?

1064
01:05:07,635 --> 01:05:11,315
To me, Kingfisher is
a psychopath, a murderer.

1065
01:05:11,315 --> 01:05:13,259
You're the family of a crime victim.

1066
01:05:13,259 --> 01:05:15,123
Can I borrow this for the weekend?

1067
01:05:15,123 --> 01:05:16,223
I have something to confess.

1068
01:05:16,223 --> 01:05:19,659
I know... who Kingfisher is.

